void printCeiling(int arr[], int n){
    System.out.println(-1);                              // first element has no left ceil

    for(int i=1;i<n;i++){                                  // traverse from second element
      int minn = Integer.MAX_VALUE;                          // track smallest valid left value

      for(int j=0;j<i;j++){                                   // check all left elements
          if(arr[i] <= arr[j]){                                 // left value is >= current
              minn = Math.min(minn,arr[j]);                       // keep smallest such value
          }
      }

      if(minn == Integer.MAX_VALUE){                          // no valid value found
          System.out.println(-1);                                // print -1
      }
      else{
          System.out.println(minn);                             // print the ceiling value
      }

    }
}

//////////////////////// DRY RUN /////////////////////////////
arr = [10, 5, 11, 6, 20, 12]

index:   0    1    2    3    4    5
value:   10   5    11   6    20   12

i=0 -> print -1

i=1 -> left:[10]         -> 10
i=2 -> left:[10,5]       -> -1
i=3 -> left:[10,5,11]    -> 10
i=4 -> left:[10,5,11,6]  -> -1
i=5 -> left:[..20]       -> 20

output: -1 10 -1 10 -1 20

//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Closest Greater or Same Value on Left Side for Every Element in Array

Given an array of integers, find the closest (not considering the distance, but value) greater or the same value on the left of every element. 
If an element has no greater or same value on the left side, print -1.

Examples

Input: arr[] = [10, 5, 11, 6, 20, 12]
Output: [-1, 10, -1, 10, -1, 20]
Explanation: The first element has nothing on the left side, so the answer is -1. The second element 5 has 10 on the left, so the answer is 10. 
The third element 11 has nothing greater or the same on the left, so the answer is -1. The fourth element 6 has 10 as the closest value wise, so the answer is 10. 
The fifth element 20 has nothing greater or the same, so the answer is -1. The sixth element 12 has 20 on the left, so the answer is 20.

Constraints:
1 ≤ arr.size() ≤ 10^6
1 ≤ arr[i] ≤ 10^6
